## Result and exclusions

The assembled, source-reviewed qualitative result is: the unconditioned planar
periodized field is almost surely Morse with distinct critical values and no
saddle-saddle gradient connection. The same holds for each fixed admissible
original two-pin law and its original full determinant tilt. Thus their planar
gradient flows are almost surely Morse-Smale, in the completed-measure sense.

Admissible pin sites are distinct on the torus, the gap is positive, and the
parameters lie in the named parent validity regime or a separately proved
extension. The theorem is per fixed law. It is not one common probability-one
set for all uncountably many targets, and provides no uniform quantitative
constants as the pins coalesce. Arbitrary pinned means still need their own
Q(Omega_gen)=1 hypothesis.

No regional C103 estimate, numerical normalizer floor, C103/R0 Boolean transition,
RN/JETMOD closure, P0.1 release, three-dimensional Morse-Smale result, quantitative
near-connection rate, or global multi-witness factorial upper bound follows from
this source integration alone. Consumer status updates require a separate exact
object/measure/radius reading and the existing byte-tracked dependency mechanism.

